---
import Menu from "./Menu.astro";
import ThemeToggle from "./ThemeToggle.astro";
import AuthButton from "./AuthButton.astro";
import { site } from "../config";

const initials = site.title
  .split(/\s+/u)
  .filter(Boolean)
  .map((word) => word[0])
  .join("")
  .toUpperCase();
---

{
  /* max-w-5xl, not the max-w-4xl the rest of the site uses. The owner allowed this on 2026-09-22,
  after the reviewer found the bar crowded: Video made a sixth menu item, and six items plus the
  title and the theme toggle inside 896px pushed everything towards the middle. 1024px gives back
  roughly what the new item took.

  This is the only element on the site wider than max-w-4xl - main and the footer in Base.astro
  keep it - so the header no longer lines up with the article card below it above 1024px. That is
  the price of the change and it was accepted. It is also a departure from the Hugo header, which
  has one width for everything; REVIEW-VIDEO.md remark 4 records the decision.

  No bespoke class was needed, although the reviewer asked for one: this wrapper has lived in this
  component since 2026-09-09 (the note at the top of the file says why), so it is already separate
  from the page's width. Tailwind's own step is the class; a hand-made one would hide the value
  from anyone reading the markup. */
}
{
  /* The side padding is trimmed between 640px and 1024px, added 2026-09-22 with the sizes in
  Menu.astro. That is the band where the whole header has to fit on one line - six menu items,
  the title, the logo and the theme switch - and it was spilling off the right edge, taking the
  switch with it. 12px a side instead of 24px is 24px back into the row. Below 640px the menu is
  a hamburger and there is nothing to squeeze, so the padding stays as it was; from 1024px the
  row fits with room to spare and the header is again what Hugo renders. */
}
<div
  class="mx-auto w-full max-w-5xl overflow-x-auto px-6 sm:overflow-visible sm:px-3 lg:px-6"
>
  <div class="flex items-center justify-between py-3">
    {
      /* max-w-[70%] below 640px instead of Hugo's max-w-[40%]: the logo takes room the
      wordmark used to have, and with 40% the title truncated to "Radiesthes...". Above 640px
      the class is still sm:max-w-md, exactly as Hugo has it. */
    }
    {
      /* min-w-0 and no flex-shrink-0 below 1024px, added 2026-09-22 with the magnifier. The icon
      costs the row about 32px, and measurement found exactly one band where that does not fit:
      from 640px, where the full menu replaces the hamburger, to 676px, the row wanted 651px
      against 616px. Everything wider fits with the sizes tightened earlier today.

      A flex child will not shrink past its content unless it is told it may - flex-shrink-0 said
      no, and min-width:auto is the default even without it - so the row could only spill. With
      both off, the name gives up as many pixels as the row is short and `truncate` ends it in an
      ellipsis: about 35px at 640px, nothing at 680px and above, because shrinking is proportional
      to need. flex-shrink-0 comes back at 1024px, where the row has room to spare and the header
      is again exactly what Hugo renders.

      The alternative, and it is the owner's to decide: keep the hamburger until 768px instead of
      640px, which removes the crowded band altogether rather than truncating anything. He chose
      640px when the menu had five items and no logo; REVIEW-VIDEO.md remark 4 has the history. */
    }
    <div
      class="min-w-0 max-w-[70%] truncate text-lg font-bold sm:max-w-md sm:text-xl lg:flex-shrink-0"
    >
      <a
        href="/"
        aria-label={site.title}
        class="text-gray-900 no-underline transition-colors hover:text-blue-600 dark:text-gray-100 dark:hover:text-blue-300"
      >
        {
          /* The avatar from the About page, doubling as a logo where the wordmark alone has
          to carry the header. Only below 640px, where the menu is a hamburger; sm:hidden
          makes it display:none above that, so the desktop header stays byte-identical to
          Hugo. It is inline-block rather than a flex child on purpose - turning the anchor
          into a flex container would change how the link itself lays out at every width.
          alt is empty because the link's own text already says the site name; announcing it
          twice is worse than not announcing the image at all. */
        }
        {
          /* Changed 2026-09-22, which makes the sentence above half true: sm:hidden is gone. The
          owner asked for the same logo at every width (REVIEW-VIDEO.md remark 5), so the desktop
          header is deliberately no longer byte-identical to Hugo's - that parity was the only
          reason the image was hidden there. It shrinks rather than disappears: h-8 w-8 below
          640px as before, h-6 w-6 from there up, about the size of a favicon, so the height of
          the bar stays decided by the text and not by the picture. */
        }
        {
          site.avatar && (
            <img
              src={site.avatar}
              alt=""
              width="32"
              height="32"
              class="mr-2 inline-block h-8 w-8 rounded-full object-cover align-middle ring-1 ring-gray-200 dark:ring-slate-700 sm:h-6 sm:w-6"
            />
          )
        }
        {
          /* Under 400px even 70% of the header cannot hold the wordmark next to the logo, and
          `truncate` turned it into "Radiesthes...", which reads worse than no wordmark at all.
          Below that width the initials stand in for it. 400px is a judgement call, not a
          measurement: it is roughly where "Radiesthesia Club" stops fitting at text-lg beside a
          32px logo, and `min-[400px]:` is an arbitrary variant so no Tailwind screen had to be
          invented for one rule. The anchor carries aria-label, so the accessible name stays the
          full site title at every width no matter which of the two spans is painted. */
        }
        <span class="min-[400px]:hidden">{initials}</span>
        <span class="hidden min-[400px]:inline">{site.title}</span>
      </a>
    </div>
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
      <Menu />
      {
        /* Changed 2026-09-22 at the owner's request: the switch stays in the bar at every width
        and no longer moves into the drop-down panel when the menu opens. It used to carry
        `hidden sm:inline-flex`, so below 640px the bar hid it and the panel showed a second
        instance under a "Theme" row; the owner asked for the arrangement in the reference he
        sent, where the switch sits in the bar beside the close button and the panel holds the
        menu and nothing else. The button is written after the hamburger now so that it is the
        last control on the row at every width, which is where it already sat on a desktop. */
      }
      {
        /* The magnifier, added 2026-09-22 with /search/. It is a link and not a button: the
        search lives at an address of its own, so it has to be openable in a new tab, and a
        visitor without JavaScript still reaches a page that explains itself. First of the three
        controls at every width - search, menu, theme - which is the order in the reference the
        owner sent. The label is on the link, since an aria-hidden icon leaves it without a name. */
      }
      {
        /* members-only, added the evening of 2026-09-25 with the guest gate (AUTH.md section 10):
        the search reads the index of the articles and the lectures, which a guest does not get,
        and the owner's header for a guest is Home, the theme switch and the sign-in icon. Hidden
        by custom.css until the gate in Base.astro marks the document kb-member; /search/ itself
        is a closed page anyway. */
      }
      {
        /* Reopened on 2026-09-25 after the colleague's review (AUTH.md section 11): the search is for everyone again. */
      }
      <a
        href="/search/"
        aria-label="Search"
        class="relative inline-flex h-7 w-7 cursor-pointer items-center justify-center text-gray-700 no-underline transition-colors hover:text-blue-600 dark:text-gray-200 dark:hover:text-blue-300"
      >
        <svg
          class="h-5 w-5"
          viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          fill="none"
          stroke="currentColor"
          stroke-width="2"
          stroke-linecap="round"
          aria-hidden="true"
        >
          <circle cx="11" cy="11" r="7"></circle>
          <path d="M20 20l-3.5-3.5"></path>
        </svg>
      </a>

      {
        /* members-only, added later on the evening of 2026-09-25 at the owner's word: a guest keeps
        the theme switch and the sign-in icon and nothing else in the bar, so the hamburger goes with
        the menu it opens (every item but Home is hidden for a guest already, and the panel would show
        one word). Hidden by custom.css until the gate in Base.astro marks the document kb-member
        (AUTH.md section 10). */
      }
      {
        /* Reopened on 2026-09-25 after the colleague's review (AUTH.md section 11): the hamburger is for everyone again. */
      }
      <button
        id="menu-toggle"
        type="button"
        class="relative inline-flex h-7 w-7 cursor-pointer items-center justify-center border-0 bg-transparent p-0 text-gray-700 focus:outline-none dark:text-gray-200 sm:hidden"
        aria-label="Open menu"
        aria-expanded="false"
        aria-controls="site-menu"
      >
        <svg
          data-menu-icon="open"
          class="h-6 w-6"
          viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          fill="none"
          stroke="currentColor"
          stroke-width="2"
          stroke-linecap="round"
          aria-hidden="true"
        >
          <path d="M4 7h16M4 12h16M4 17h16"></path>
        </svg>
        <svg
          data-menu-icon="close"
          class="hidden h-6 w-6"
          viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          fill="none"
          stroke="currentColor"
          stroke-width="2"
          stroke-linecap="round"
          aria-hidden="true"
        >
          <path d="M6 6l12 12M18 6L6 18"></path>
        </svg>
      </button>

      {
        /* ml-1 below 1024px, ml-2 above: at exactly 640px, where the menu appears, the row was
        still 3px wider than the space it had. Measured, like the rest of this band. */
      }
      <ThemeToggle class="ml-1 inline-flex lg:ml-2" />
      <AuthButton />
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div id="site-menu" class="sm:hidden" hidden>
  {
    /* Widened with the bar above on 2026-09-22 so the two cannot drift apart. Nothing visible
    changes here: the panel only exists below 640px, where the viewport is narrower than either
    limit and mx-auto has nothing to centre. */
  }
  <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-5xl px-6 pb-4">
    <Menu variant="panel" />
    {
      /* The "Theme" row that stood here - a label and a second ThemeToggle - was removed on
      2026-09-22 with the change above. The panel holds the menu and nothing else now, and the
      document carries one theme button instead of two, so nothing has to be kept in sync
      between them. */
    }
  </div>
</div>
